# Story 69: Pane Listening (50s)
# Hook: Pipe one pane's live output straight into another -- secrets redacted automatically.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-069-pane-listening.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Pipe one pane's live output straight into another -- secrets redacted automatically.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh and split a second pane. We'll have one pane listen to the other.

[00:08.0 --> 00:18.0]
In the left pane, switch to rysh mode and give it a name so the listener has an alias to attach to.

[00:18.0 --> 00:28.0]
Move to the other pane and run pane listen builder. Now the builder's shared output flows here, prefixed [builder].

[00:28.0 --> 00:40.0]
Back in the builder, run a command. Its output appears in the listening pane in real time -- secrets stripped first.

[00:40.0 --> 00:47.0]
When you're done, the listening pane runs pane unlisten to detach the stream.

[00:47.0 --> 00:50.0]
Cross-pane awareness with redaction built in.

